=== F-01 reproduction: key rotation without key identifiers ===
key A generated (ML-DSA-65)
Release 1.0 signed with key A; verify under A: VALID
key rotated: A -> B (old key discarded by the pipeline)
Release 2.0 signed with key B; verify under B: VALID
Release 1.0 (untouched) verified under current key B: INVALID
Release 1.0 (TAMPERED) verified under current key B: INVALID
artifact sha256 v1: 2c0cf9149349f939... (unchanged — the artifact is intact)

REPRODUCED: after rotation, an intact previously signed artifact
fails verification, and the failure is identical to a tampered
artifact's failure. The pipeline cannot tell rotation from
tampering because signatures carry no key identifier.
